.TH STUDIO 1 "October 2026" "vst-ace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
studio \- the session window: a tab per plug\-in, beside the tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B studio
.RI [ \-\-synth " plug\-in" "]... [" \-\-tracker "] [" \-\-song " file.trk] [" \-\-quit\-after " ms]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B studio
is the vst\-ace session window. It opens on a blank canvas; File > New synth
opens a tab hosting one plug\-in \(em the full pestudio host, with its
programs, parameters, keyboard, patch banks and editor \(em and File > New
tracker opens the pattern sequencer in a tab of its own. Only the tab in front
answers the computer keyboard, and each synth tab gets its own audio stream
and MIDI port, so several plug\-ins play at once.
.PP
Plug\-ins built for Windows, macOS and Linux all load as native code; there is
no Wine and no emulation. They are hosted out of process by default, so one
that faults costs a helper rather than the session.
.PP
The tracker tab is the same tracker the standalone binary runs, one per
process; the windows a song's tracks play can be the synth tabs beside it.
.SH OPTIONS
A session can be named rather than clicked together. Each
.B \-\-synth
opens a synth tab with that plug\-in loaded,
.B \-\-tracker
opens the tracker tab, and
.B \-\-song
loads a song into it, opening the tab first if needed.
.B \-\-quit\-after
quits that many milliseconds later, for scripted runs. With no arguments the
window opens on the blank canvas.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Editors embed through an X11 window id, so this wants to be \fBxcb\fR under
Wayland; XWayland is enough. Override it for a native Wayland window and no
native editors.
.TP
.B PEHOST_ISOLATE
Set to 0 to host in process rather than behind the helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR va (1),
.BR pestudio (1),
.BR peload (1),
.BR dwstudio (1).
